  "read_laws": [
    "All 17 predicates leave context, frames, pointed objects and caller memory unchanged. No external effects or error callbacks.",
    "The Never variant performs no reads. Group mismatches avoid all frame reads except CaptureOperation, ObjectOperation, AlternateObjectOperation and ProcessingOperation, which evaluate canonical current operation first.",
    "Format predicates read frame+0x530 only for matching groups. Plane predicates read frame+0x3228 then pointed+0x110 only for matching groups. HalfwordModeSplit reads exactly unsigned halfword frame+0x1682.",
    "Operation predicates evaluate canonical e93760/e9371c getter before group filtering and reload context frame afterward. Getter reads context+4 first; kind7 selects frame+0x38; otherwise frame+0x4b4 selects frame+0 for mode29, or frame+4*(context+0x34-11) with wrapping A32 address arithmetic.",
    "CaptureOperation reads mode578, then short-circuits 4a8/550 or 5a8/4a8/550/4ac/614/61c in original order. ObjectOperation reads 578 then63c then byte19b4; alternate omits63c. ProcessingOperation reads4a8.",
    "Feature predicates read word2fb8 or2fbc. Correction predicates read frame+3098 then pointed+58; if equal1 read frame+4b4, then5b8 only mode25 or5b4 only mode26.",
    "GroupModeSplit and OutputModeSplit read63c only for accepted group candidates. Every published predicate result is canonical, including rsbs/movlo zero tests.",
    "Repeated calls re-read mutable inputs. There is no cached frame or policy result across calls and no CPU FFI boundary inside these predicates."
  ],
